---
name: land
description: The land lane as the sub-workflow the execute phase calls.
type: subworkflow
icon: flow.land
entry: start
exit: done
exit: handed_back
modification_date: 2026-01-15
version: 0.1.0
author: plan-marshall
---
# The land lane, written for the invariant and unit-loader tests, never copied from the product. It is a sub-workflow
# of the execute phase (called through the phase's `land` entry), never a phase of its own: a lane is a choice of
# phases. The worktree initialization precedes the verify sweep, which precedes the exit barrier out of the lane.
workflow land version 1 format 1
scope subworkflow
entry start -> land.worktree-init

state land.worktree-init
    auto test.proceed
        done -> land.verify-sweep

state land.verify-sweep
    job test.build
        succeeded -> land.exit-barrier
        failed -> land.hand-back-exit
        cancelled -> land.hand-back-exit

state land.exit-barrier
    auto test.proceed
        done -> land.done-exit

state land.done-exit terminal done success

state land.hand-back-exit terminal handed_back failure
